description:
I'm currently using `pkgdown` to host all the documentation for my work's internal R packages. Currently, `downlit` just defaults to using https://rdrr.io for packages/documentation without a package-defined URL. This works fine if your package is publicly available, but because all of these packages are internal and so hosted on our internal network rather than CRAN, users just get sent to a dead link.

We do however have a consistent internal structure for the documentation of these internal packages (like https://rdrr.io but just for these packages), meaning that links could easily be generated for these internal packages.

It would be really helpful to be able to change the default link. Ideally this would be for selected packages, but I think that would be much tougher to implement.

Straight away I was thinking that implementing some kind of `downlit.default.host` option and some variable substitution would provide the functionality. For example, by setting the option to "https://my-custom-host/packages/%s/docs" and changing the `href_package_ref ()` function from:

```
    if (is_base_package(package)) {
      paste0("https://rdrr.io/r/", package)
    } else {
      paste0("https://rdrr.io/pkg/", package, "/man")
    }
```

to

```
...
    if (is_base_package(package)) {
      sprintf("https://rdrr.io/r/%s", package)
    } else {
      sprintf(getOption("downlit.default.host", "https://rdrr.io/pkg/%s/man"), package)
    }
...
```

But this would then change every link where the parent package doesn't have a custom URL to that new host. That might be okay for some but then it's also quite limiting.

Happy to work on a PR and any thoughts would be appreciated.
